&& L1 VERIFY -- can WORKSPACE DELETE reach a name that has NO runtime workspace?
&& AIF-078 lifecycle lane. The plan asserts this from PG_T4's note, not from a run.
&&
&& IT NEVER TOUCHES THE PRODUCTION CATALOG. It composes L0's proven lever: the
&& WORKSPACES slot is redirected to a fresh scratch root first, so every mint,
&& retire and delete below lands in a throwaway catalog. Production is not read
&& and not written.
&&
&& TWO ARMS, in opposite directions, because "DELETE reached it" and "DELETE
&& refused what it should refuse" are different claims and a half-fix shows one:
&&   L1A  minted, DESTROYed (so it is catalog-only), then DELETEd  -> expect SUCCESS
&&   L1B  minted and left LIVE in this session, then DELETEd       -> expect REFUSAL

SETPATH WORKSPACES D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\tmp\wscat_l1

ECHO === arm A: mint, then retire, so the name is CATALOG-ONLY ===
WORKSPACE NEW L1A
WORKSPACE DESTROY L1A

ECHO === arm B: mint and LEAVE IT LIVE in this session ===
WORKSPACE NEW L1B

ECHO === catalog before any DELETE ===
USE D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\tmp\wscat_l1\WORKSPACES.dbf
COUNT
COUNT FOR SUPERSEDED = "1"
COUNT FOR SUPERSEDED = "0"

ECHO === A: DELETE a retired, catalog-only name -- expect it to REACH it ===
WORKSPACE DELETE L1A

ECHO === B: DELETE a name still declared in this session -- expect REFUSAL ===
WORKSPACE DELETE L1B

ECHO === after: rows are FLAGGED, never packed, so the file does not shrink ===
USE D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\tmp\wscat_l1\WORKSPACES.dbf
COUNT
ECHO --- and with SET DELETED OFF the flagged rows are still there ---
SET DELETED OFF
COUNT
SET DELETED ON

ECHO === restore and confirm ===
SETPATH WORKSPACES D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\workspaces
SETPATH
